    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] Peter Murphy (7 March 1922 – 7 April 1975), often referred to as \"Spud\" Murphy, was an English footballer who played as an inside left.\n[2] Bernhard Carl \"Bert\" Trautmann OBE (22 October 1923 – 19 July 2013) was a German professional footballer who played as a goalkeeper for Manchester City from 1949 to 1964.\n[3] He played for Birmingham City from 1943 to 1959, making 443 appearances in all competitions and scoring 3 goals, and played in the 1956 FA Cup final which Birmingham lost to Manchester City 3–1.\n[4] He is possibly best remembered for the incident in the 1956 FA Cup Final when Manchester City's goalkeeper Bert Trautmann broke a bone in his neck when diving at Murphy's feet."
